# The image build needs exactly three inputs, so this file is a whitelist
# rather than a list of things to skip. A blocklist rots: it goes stale the
# first time someone adds a top-level directory, and the failure is silent --
# the build still succeeds, just with more context than it needed.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole repository. Measured before adding
# it: 1163.9 MiB sent to the daemon against 0.09 MiB the Dockerfile actually
# copies, because `server/target/` is 1160 MiB after any local `cargo build`.
# `.gitignore` does not help here; Docker does not read it.
#
# It also kept `rasen/` out of the build context. That directory is a separate
# Git repository with its own remote, and nothing about the image build should
# be able to see it.
*

!server/Cargo.toml
!server/Cargo.lock
!server/src
